---
import LegalPage from '@/components/LegalPage.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '@/lib/config';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Affiliate Disclosure"
  description="How affiliate links work on The Ludarium, in plain language. We may earn a small commission, it never costs you more, and it never decides what we recommend."
  lede="Some links on this site earn us a small commission. Here is exactly how that works."
  updated="October 16, 2026"
>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    When we link to a game, book, or service, that link is sometimes an affiliate link. If you buy
    something after clicking it, the seller may pay The Ludarium a small commission.
    <strong>It never costs you anything extra.</strong>
  </p>

  <h2>Why we use them</h2>
  <p>
    Affiliate commissions help pay for free guides and free game tools, and they help fund our first
    game lounge. We do not run display ads, so this is one of the quiet ways the site supports itself.
  </p>

  <h2>Our promise</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We only recommend things we believe will genuinely help you and your table.</li>
    <li>A commission never decides what we recommend or how we rate it.</li>
    <li>If a publisher gives us a free copy of a game, we will say so in the article.</li>
    <li>Articles with affiliate links say so near the top, with a link to this page.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How affiliate links are marked</h2>
  <p>
    Affiliate links open in a new tab and are labeled as sponsored for search engines. When you click
    one, the seller may use a cookie to remember that you came from The Ludarium. Their own privacy
    policy covers that cookie.
  </p>

  <h2>Our own products</h2>
  <p>
    When we mention something from <a href="/store/">The Ludarium store</a>, like an RPG Demo Library
    adventure, that is our own product, not an affiliate link.
  </p>

  <h2>Programs we belong to</h2>
  <p>
    The Ludarium is a participant in the Amazon Services LLC Associates Program, an affiliate
    advertising program that lets sites earn fees by linking to Amazon.com. As an Amazon Associate,
    The Ludarium earns from qualifying purchases.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    {
      CONTACT_EMAIL ? (
        <>
          Ask us anything about this at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
        </>
      ) : (
        <>Ask us anything about this by replying to any email from The Ludarium.</>
      )
    }
  </p>
</LegalPage>
